          "guid": "mszscb0mn38yn8zj",
          "message": {
            "text": "mode:'replace' needs to dismiss the region's OTHER toasts, but that active set is stored ON the region element (a Symbol prop), not in a module-level variable — so toast() keeps zero module state, consistent with toastRegion() which already keeps \"the region\" in the DOM rather than a module singleton.\n\nA mode:'replace' toast can't just region.innerHTML = '' to clear the others: that would strip their DOM without running each one's mount() disposer (leaking the mount) and without honoring an in-flight exitClass transition. It needs their real dismiss fns. The obvious place to keep them is a module-level WeakMap<region, Set<dismiss>>, but that reintroduces module-level mutable state this file was designed to avoid (Design rule 5). Hanging the Set off the region element via region[TOAST_SET] puts the state where its lifetime already lives — GC'd with the region, scoped per region for free (a custom container gets its own set), and invisible to grep '^let'. Iterating a COPY ([...active]) before dismissing matters: each dismiss calls active.delete(itself), which would corrupt a live iteration.\n",
            "markdown": "`mode:'replace'` needs to dismiss the region's OTHER toasts, but that active set is stored ON the region element (a Symbol prop), not in a module-level variable — so toast() keeps zero module state, consistent with `toastRegion()` which already keeps \"the region\" in the DOM rather than a module singleton.\n\nA `mode:'replace'` toast can't just `region.innerHTML = ''` to clear the others: that would strip their DOM without running each one's `mount()` disposer (leaking the mount) and without honoring an in-flight `exitClass` transition. It needs their real `dismiss` fns. The obvious place to keep them is a module-level `WeakMap<region, Set<dismiss>>`, but that reintroduces module-level mutable state this file was designed to avoid (Design rule 5). Hanging the `Set` off the region element via `region[TOAST_SET]` puts the state where its lifetime already lives — GC'd with the region, scoped per region for free (a custom `container` gets its own set), and invisible to `grep '^let'`. Iterating a COPY (`[...active]`) before dismissing matters: each `dismiss` calls `active.delete(itself)`, which would corrupt a live iteration.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/overlay.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 838,
                  "endLine": 842,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "\n  const region = toastRegion(container) as ToastCarrier;\n  const active = (region[TOAST_SET] ??= new Set<() => void>());\n  if (mode === 'replace') for (const d of [...active]) d(); // collapse-to-latest\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
