          "guid": "mszsnm5xs9u27k44",
          "message": {
            "text": "The BYO render API is small because the dialogs were already wired by DATA ATTRIBUTE, not by class — render only swaps the body; nothing in the resolve/validate path changed.\n\nconfirm/prompt/form delegate on [data-confirm] / [data-prompt] / [data-form] and look up fields via [data-prompt-input] / [data-field] / [data-field-error]. So supporting caller-supplied markup needed exactly three things, none of them touching the promise/validate/Enter logic: (1) branch body to the caller's render(slots) when provided; (2) hand the caller the wiring as spreadable attribute bags (ok: { 'data-confirm': 'ok' }, etc.) so their elements carry the same hooks; (3) move initialFocus from the kerf class selectors (.kerf-confirm__ok) to the data-attribute selectors ([data-confirm=\"ok\"]) so focus lands in BYO markup too. The one behavioral softening: the error slot became optional (nullable-guarded in prompt/form) because a design-system dialog without validate shouldn't be forced to include an error element — covered by the \"render without an error slot\" tests, which exercise the null arms the default-markup tests can't reach.\n",
            "markdown": "The BYO `render` API is small because the dialogs were already wired by DATA ATTRIBUTE, not by class — `render` only swaps the body; nothing in the resolve/validate path changed.\n\n`confirm`/`prompt`/`form` delegate on `[data-confirm]` / `[data-prompt]` / `[data-form]` and look up fields via `[data-prompt-input]` / `[data-field]` / `[data-field-error]`. So supporting caller-supplied markup needed exactly three things, none of them touching the promise/validate/Enter logic: (1) branch `body` to the caller's `render(slots)` when provided; (2) hand the caller the wiring as spreadable attribute bags (`ok: { 'data-confirm': 'ok' }`, etc.) so their elements carry the same hooks; (3) move `initialFocus` from the kerf class selectors (`.kerf-confirm__ok`) to the data-attribute selectors (`[data-confirm=\"ok\"]`) so focus lands in BYO markup too. The one behavioral softening: the error slot became optional (nullable-guarded in prompt/form) because a design-system dialog without `validate` shouldn't be forced to include an error element — covered by the \"render without an error slot\" tests, which exercise the null arms the default-markup tests can't reach.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
